From 2f59a9b80c6ab81cb8bd6a4c02b17b90a6506ea9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Icenowy Zheng <zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 16:14:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 043/468] FROMGIT: arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp-crd: set GPI DMA
 channels

It's found that some GPI interfaces shouldn't be touched by HLOS,
otherwise system hang / reset happens.

The GPI interface availability information is available via the ACPI
DSDT table, as interrupt resources for \_SB_.QGP* devices.

Add such information to the device tree file.

The DSDT table is acquired by extraction of qcfirmware8280_NVME.cab file
version 200.0.68.0 from Windows Update.

Signed-off-by: Icenowy Zheng <zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260602081451.3808833-2-zhengxingda@iscas.ac.cn
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <andersson@kernel.org>

(cherry picked from commit 63f13ee5a595a160433b3f1a6c8f0b5c1716cc1e
 https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/qcom/linux.git for-next)
Signed-off-by: Kexy Biscuit <kexybiscuit@aosc.io>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-crd.dts | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-crd.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-crd.dts
index 1eea9d710d5b2..f4af4f2b6827d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-crd.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp-crd.dts
@@ -493,14 +493,17 @@ &dispcc0 {
 };
 
 &gpi_dma0 {
+	dma-channel-mask = <0x3>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &gpi_dma1 {
+	dma-channel-mask = <0x3>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &gpi_dma2 {
+	dma-channel-mask = <0x3>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
